# STRYV - .gitignore
# Conservative: excludes only build output, dependencies, logs and local
# editor/OS clutter. Application source, configuration, branding and required
# assets are all intentionally tracked.

# --- Dependencies -----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# --- Tauri / Rust build output ----------------------------------------------
src-tauri/target/
# Generated by `tauri android` / `tauri ios` (not used by this Windows app,
# but never commit generated platform scaffolding).
src-tauri/gen/

# --- Mobile icon sets --------------------------------------------------------
# `tauri icon` emits Android and iOS icon sets alongside the desktop ones.
# STRYV is a Windows-only desktop app: there is no src-tauri/gen/, no mobile
# project, and tauri.conf.json declares no mobile configuration, so these 35
# files (288 KB) would never be used. They stay on disk (regenerate any time
# with `npx tauri icon src-tauri/icons/icon.png`) but are not tracked.
# If a mobile target is ever added, delete these two lines and commit the sets.
src-tauri/icons/android/
src-tauri/icons/ios/

# --- Frontend / bundler output ----------------------------------------------
dist/

# --- Logs -------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Local environment overrides (no backend/network calls today; guard anyway)
.env
.env.local

# --- Signing keys (NEVER commit these) ---------------------------------------
# The updater's private key belongs in the GitHub Actions secret
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY only. Losing it means you can never sign another
# update for the installs that already exist.
.tauri/
*.key
*.key.pub
*.sig

# --- Editor / OS clutter -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY *NOT* IGNORED - do not add these:
#
#   Cargo.lock          - STRYV is an APPLICATION, not a library. The lockfile
#                         MUST be committed once `cargo build` generates it, so
#                         that Rust dependency versions are reproducible. It does
#                         not exist yet only because the project has never been
#                         built in place.
#   package-lock.json   - Same reason, for the npm dependency tree.
#   *.png / *.ico        - Required application and bundler icons. `src/assets/*`
#                         are loaded at runtime by index.html; `src-tauri/icons/*`
#                         is required by `tauri.conf.json` -> bundle.icon.
#   brand/              - Source branding assets (SVG + emblem).
#   src-tauri/tauri.conf.json, src-tauri/capabilities/ - App configuration.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  # Regenerated by make-context-bundle.ps1 - a paste bundle, not source.
  CONTEXT-BUNDLE.txt
  # Regenerated by make-context-bundle.ps1 - a paste bundle, not source.
  CONTEXT-BUNDLE.txt
